{
  "about": "What each reply move DOES, so that 'four different answers' is something a test can read (owner, Oct 27, 4 PM Eastern: \"four replies are four different answers, never one reworded\"; Oct 14, afternoon: \"Four dynamic choices, always\"; Oct 15, evening: \"The four replies each move the talk somewhere\"). A turn offers one reply per group, never two wordings of one answer. Moves only: no sentence is here. `everyday` is by the bank subject a reply answers, then its choice (data/english/parts/conversation.json); `scene` is by the move name a scene with a purpose offers (purpose-arcs.json, data/english/parts/scene-talk.json). A move with no group fails tests/director-reply-meanings.test.ts.",
  "groups": {
    "answers": "Answers the question plainly and nothing more.",
    "adds": "Answers and adds a fact from the player's own record (how long, where, since when).",
    "turns-back": "Turns the question back on the other person.",
    "deflects": "Puts the question off, or leaves it unanswered without refusing.",
    "agrees": "Agrees, accepts or says the same.",
    "refuses": "Declines to answer or to do it.",
    "disagrees": "Says it is not so, or sees it differently.",
    "asks": "Asks for more or for a reason.",
    "acknowledges": "Takes the line in and lets the other person carry on.",
    "reacts": "Reacts to what was said (surprise, a first feeling).",
    "comforts": "Offers sympathy or reassurance.",
    "hopes": "Says what the player hopes or expects will happen.",
    "helps": "Asks how to help, or says the player will help.",
    "promises": "Promises to stand by or to do it.",
    "offers": "Puts something on the table (a job, money, a hand).",
    "requests": "Asks the other person for something.",
    "presses": "Pushes again for what the player wants.",
    "thanks": "Thanks the other person.",
    "congratulates": "Congratulates the other person.",
    "tells": "Tells something that happened.",
    "opines": "Gives a view of the matter.",
    "admits": "Admits to it.",
    "apologizes": "Says sorry.",
    "confronts": "Pushes back, blames or warns.",
    "bargains": "Offers a trade or a condition.",
    "boasts": "Plays up the player's own standing.",
    "lies": "Says what is not so.",
    "leaves": "Ends the talk by going.",
    "changes-subject": "Moves the talk to something else, with a short answer or none."
  },
  "fill": {
    "about": "The groups a new move fills a short set with when the spot's own moves cannot reach four (the words-engine skill: \"Fill a gap with a new move (a reply that adds a fact from the player's own record, turns it back, deflects, declines)\"; the item's Notes, Nov 10: home-new \"has no move that adds a detail from the player's record, deflects, or changes the subject\"; #8174 wrote a change-the-subject answer for own-work and mutual). Read by the words run (`npm run words:rules`), which names them, after the spot's own unwritten moves, as the groups a gap in data/english/pulled.json is missing. Never read by play.",
    "groups": ["adds", "turns-back", "deflects", "changes-subject", "refuses"]
  },
